// Every problem the validator should report in this file is marked with an "expect" comment,
// either on the line itself or as "expect-next" on the line above it.
// The test fails if a marked problem isn't reported, or an unmarked one is.

title: Mom_L1_Lines
---
Mom: fine line #delay:2
no sender here // expect: missing-sender
"John Doe": quoted // expect: quoted-sender
John Doe: one
John Doe: two
john doe: three // expect: speaker-spelling
Mom: bad bracket [sic] // expect: unescaped-bracket
Mom: escaped is fine \[sic\] and \#hash and \/\/ and lol(
Mom: see http://x // expect: unescaped-comment
Mom: bad tag #bogus // expect: unknown-tag
Mom: bad delay #delay:0 // expect: bad-tag-value
Mom: timeout on a message #timeout:5 // expect: tag-placement
Me: delay on a typed line #delay:2 // expect: tag-placement
<<shake 3>> // expect: unknown-command
<<if made_up()>> // expect: unknown-function
    Mom: inside if
<<endif>>
Mom: {made_up_two()} // expect: unknown-function
<<declare $stray = 1>> // expect: declare-outside-variables
<<start_thread Dad Dad_L1_Missing>> // expect: unknown-node
<<set $tursted to 1>> // expect: compiler-warning
<<jump Nowhere>> // expect: compiler-warning
===

title: Mom_L1_Choices
---
-> No typed line // expect: missing-me-line, multiple-timeouts
    Mom: oops
-> Fine
    Me: ok
-> (no reply) #timeout:5
    Mom: first timeout
-> (no reply again) #timeout:6
    Mom: second timeout
Mom: after the choices
-> One // expect: too-many-choices
    Me: one
-> Two
    Me: two
-> Three
    Me: three
-> Four
    Me: four
-> Five
    Me: five
Mom: after five
-> (no reply) #timeout:3 // expect: no-visible-choices
    Mom: only a timeout
Mom: nested choices
-> Outer
    Me: outer
    -> Inner without typed line // expect: missing-me-line
        Mom: hmm
    -> Inner fine
        Me: fine
-> Choice with delay #delay:2 // expect: tag-placement
    Me: typed
===

